.\" Manpage for skyline
.\" Contact: https://github.com/antoine/skyline
.TH SKYLINE 1 "July 2026" "skyline 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skyline \- native Wayland status bar with modular islands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skyline
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B skyline
\fB\-\-write\-example\-config\fR
.br
.B skyline
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skyline
is a Wayland status bar for compositors that implement
.B wlr-layer-shell
(niri, Hyprland, Sway, and others). It draws modular
.I islands
on each monitor with workspaces, window titles, a clock, resource meters,
network status, volume and brightness controls, custom command modules, and a
StatusNotifierItem system tray.
.PP
Skyline is written in Rust using
.B iced
and
.B iced_layershell
(no GTK, no Electron).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load configuration from
.IR PATH
instead of the default config file.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-example\-config
Write a starter configuration to
.I ~/.config/skyline/config.toml
(creating parent directories as needed) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIRI_SOCKET
When set, Skyline uses the niri IPC event stream for workspaces and windows.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
When set (and niri is not detected), Skyline uses the Hyprland IPC backend.
.TP
.B SKYLINE_OUTPUT
If set to a Wayland output name (for example
.BR DP-1 ),
Skyline binds to that output only. Otherwise it opens a bar on all outputs.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls log filtering via
.BR tracing-subscriber
(for example
.BR skyline=debug,system_tray=warn ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/skyline/config.toml
User configuration (TOML). Created by
.B \-\-write\-example\-config
or
.BR "make config" .
The running bar watches this file and hot-reloads on save
(theme, modules, separators, scroll steps, bar geometry, clock
format, sys refresh, and custom modules). Changing the compositor
backend still requires a restart.
.TP
.I target/release/skyline
Local release binary from
.BR "make"
/
.BR "make run"
(no root install).
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/skyline
Optional user install from
.BR "make install-user" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is TOML. Important keys:
.TP
.B [bar]
.BR height ,
.BR margin
(top,right,bottom,left),
.BR exclusive_zone
(pixels reserved so windows stay below/above the bar; use
.B 0
for floating islands),
.BR anchor
(\fItop\fR or \fIbottom\fR),
.BR output ,
.BR padding ,
.BR island_gap ,
.BR separators
(boolean; draw separators between modules),
.BR separator
(string glyph, default
.BR │ ),
.BR tray_menu_gap
(pixels between the bar and a tray context menu; default
.BR 4 ).
.TP
.B [theme]
RGBA float arrays in 0..=1 for
.BR background ,
.BR island_background ,
.BR text ,
.BR muted ,
.BR accent ,
.BR danger ,
.BR separator ,
plus
.BR island_radius ,
.BR island_padding
(vertical, horizontal; shared by every module island),
.BR font_size ,
.BR font
(UI family; empty = system default),
.BR emoji_font
(volume/brightness glyphs; empty = same as
.BR font ),
.BR meter_height ,
.BR meter_width ,
.BR meter_gap ,
and
.BR meter_bars
(cava-style CPU/RAM/GPU meters).
Per-meter
.B [modules.cpu]
/
.B memory
/
.B gpu
support
.BR label
and
.BR format
with tokens
.BR {label} ,
.BR {bar}
(or
.BR {meter} ),
and
.BR {percent}
(or
.BR {pct} ).
.TP
.B [modules]
.BR left ,
.BR center ,
and
.BR right
are arrays of module names:
.BR workspaces ,
.BR taskbar ,
.BR window ,
.BR clock ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR memory ,
.BR gpu ,
.BR network ,
.BR volume ,
.BR brightness ,
.BR tray ,
or
.BI custom: id .
.br
.BR tray
enables the system tray host.
.TP
.B [modules.volume]
.BR step
(scroll fraction of full scale, default
.BR 0.02 ),
.BR max_percent
(soft ceiling, default
.BR 150.0 ),
.BR detect_bluetooth
(when true, show a headset glyph if the default sink is a Bluetooth/bluez
device),
.BR show_device ,
.BR show_percent .
.TP
.B [modules.brightness]
.BR step
(percent points per scroll notch, default
.BR 2.0 )
and
.BR show_percent .
.TP
.B [modules.window]
.B max_chars
truncates the focused window title.
.TP
.B [modules.taskbar]
Icon strip of open windows on the active workspace of each monitor.
.BR width
(uniform square wrapper size in logical pixels; the strip grows with icon count),
.BR padding
(inset between wrapper and icon),
.BR gap ,
and
.BR max_items .
Left-click focuses the window (niri / Hyprland).
.TP
.B [modules.network]
.B show_strength
toggles signal percent when available.
.TP
.B on_click / on_right_click
Most module sections accept optional shell commands run on left or right
click (via
.BR sh\~\-c ).
Volume left-click still mutes when
.B on_click
is unset. Workspace left-click still focuses, and also runs
.B on_click
when set. Tray icons keep native SNI activate / menu actions.
.TP
.B [modules.sys]
.B refresh_ms
controls how often CPU/RAM/GPU meters sample (default
.BR 500 ).
.TP
.B [[modules.custom]]
Custom command islands:
.BR id ,
.BR command ,
.BR args ,
.BR interval_ms ,
optional
.BR on_click ,
and
.BR json
(when true, read a
.B text
field from JSON stdout).
.TP
.B [compositor]
.B backend
may be
.BR auto ,
.BR niri ,
.BR hyprland ,
or
.BR none .
.SH INTERACTIONS
.TP
Workspaces
Left-click focuses the workspace (niri or Hyprland).
.TP
Volume
Scroll to change volume;
click to mute/unmute. Updates are pushed in real time via PulseAudio
subscription (or a fast
.B wpctl
poll fallback). When
.B detect_bluetooth
is enabled and the default sink is Bluetooth, the module shows a headset
glyph instead of speaker emojis.
.TP
Brightness
Scroll to adjust via
.BR brightnessctl (1)
.RI ( brightnessctl\ -m
to read,
.B brightnessctl set N%+/N%-
to change). Polled for external changes.
.TP
Tray
Left-click activates the item; right-click opens its DBusMenu as an overlay.
Icons prefer named theme icons (and desktop-file fallbacks), then SNI pixmaps.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build and run from the source tree:
.PP
.nf
.RS
make run
.RE
.fi
.PP
Optional user install (no sudo; default
.BR ~/.local ):
.PP
.nf
.RS
make install-user
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start with niri:
.PP
.nf
.RS
spawn-at-startup "skyline"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Pin to one output:
.PP
.nf
.RS
SKYLINE_OUTPUT=DP-1 skyline
.RE
.fi
.SH BUGS
Report issues at the project repository. Some StatusNotifierItem clients omit
optional properties such as
.BR IconPixmap ;
Skyline treats those as non-fatal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR niri (1),
.BR hyprland (1),
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR brightnessctl (1),
.BR nmcli (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Skyline contributors
